Day 33 – Introduction to HTML

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on the fundamentals of HTML (HyperText Markup Language) and how web pages are structured. The mentor explained the basic layout of an HTML document and how different elements are used to display content on a webpage.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to HTML

HTML is used to create the structure of web pages.

It consists of elements represented by tags.

Web browsers interpret HTML to display content visually.

2️⃣ Structure of an HTML Document

The basic structure of an HTML page includes:

<html> → Root element

<head> → Contains metadata (title, links, etc.)

<body> → Contains visible content

3️⃣ Common HTML Tags

The mentor introduced basic tags:

<h1> to <h6> → Headings

<p> → Paragraph

<a> → Anchor (links)

<img> → Images

These tags help organize and display content properly on a webpage.

